  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an integer xxx, define its digit space DxD_xDx​ to be the set of all positive integers whose decimal representation is a rearrangement of the decimal representation of xxx, when written without leading zeros.\n\nFor example, if x=2024x = 2024x=2024, then Dx={4022,4202,4220,2042,2024,2402,2420,2204,2240}D_x = \\{4022, 4202, 4220, 2042, 2024, 2402, 2420, 2204, 2240\\}Dx​={4022,4202,4220,2042,2024,2402,2420,2204,2240}.\n\nFor two integers xxx and yyy, define f(x,y)f(x, y)f(x,y) to be the maximum **prime** number that divides both xxx and yyy.\n\nIf no prime divides both xxx and yyy, we say f(x,y)=1f(x, y) = 1f(x,y)=1 instead.\n\nFor instance, f(35,105)=7f(35, 105) = 7f(35,105)=7 and f(2,3)=1f(2, 3) = 1f(2,3)=1.\n\nYou are given two integers XXX and YYY.\n\nCompute the maximum value of f(a,b)f(a, b)f(a,b) across all (a,b)(a, b)(a,b) such that a∈DXa\\in D_Xa∈DX​ and b∈DYb\\in D_Yb∈DY​.\n\nThat is, compute the maximum possible common prime factor of two numbers, such that one is a rearrangement of XXX and the other is a rearrangement of YYY.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of single line of input, containing two space-separated integers XXX and YYY.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible value of f(a,b)f(a, b)f(a,b) where a∈DXa\\in D_Xa∈DX​ and b∈DYb\\in D_Yb∈DY​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2001 \\leq T \\leq 2001≤T≤200",
      "1≤X,Y&lt;1071 \\leq X,Y \\lt 10^71≤X,Y&lt;107"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
