        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We have D51={15,51}D_{51} = \\{15, 51\\}D51​={15,51} and D5={5}D_5 = \\{5\\}D5​={5}.\nIt's best to choose a=15a = 15a=15 and b=5b = 5b=5, which gives f(15,5)=5f(15, 5) = 5f(15,5)=5.\nTest case 222: We have D433={433,343,334}D_{433} = \\{433, 343, 334\\}D433​={433,343,334} and D24={24,42}D_{24} = \\{24, 42\\}D24​={24,42}.\nIt's optimal to choose a=343a = 343a=343 and b=42b = 42b=42, giving f(a,b)=7f(a, b) = 7f(a,b)=7.\nTest case 333: We have D55={55}D_{55} = \\{55\\}D55​={55} and D100={100}D_{100} = \\{100\\}D100​={100}.\nOur only choice is f(55,100)=5f(55, 100) = 5f(55,100)=5.\nTest case 444: We have D2={2}D_{2} = \\{2\\}D2​={2} and D3={3}D_{3} = \\{3\\}D3​={3}.\nOur only choice is f(2,3)=1f(2, 3) = 1f(2,3)=1. (Note that 222 and 333 are coprime.)"
      }
